      "message": "Can we avoid gralloc in `libplatform`?  It should really be renamed `libplatform_virtgpu` since the goal is abstract out guest virtio-gpu, and not be a center for all platform specific code [we already have some of that, see `guest/fuchsia` and `guest/mesa/src/util`.  Plan is to move `fuchsia` stuff into Mesa util and upstream that].  I guess a good place to put Gralloc/ANativeWindow would be perhaps `./guest/gralloc_cb`?\n\nThough, it does make sense for the Gralloc to access the `EmulatedVirtioGpu` singleton.\n\nI also think RutabagaLayer eventually should be moved to its own shared library, while `libplatform_virtgpu` should be static but called the `EmulatedVirtioGpu` singleton.  The reason is `SnapshotSaveAndLoad` calls `stream_renderer_*` functions directly.  Those snapshot apis should also be only accessed through the `EmulatedVirtioGpu` singleton.  The reason is then we can migrate to the librutabaga_ffi.so, which doesn\u0027t maintain a singleton like `stream_renderer_*.`",
